## Summary
Norway's energy minister has warned the EU against pushing its green agenda, vowing to continue oil and gas drilling in the Arctic. He rejected the long-standing characterization of Norway as Europe's 'green battery,' signaling a shift away from renewable energy commitments in favor of fossil fuel extraction.

## Key Points
- Norway's energy minister explicitly warned the EU against advancing its green agenda
- Norway vows to continue drilling for oil and gas in the Arctic region
- The minister rejected Norway's long-standing image as Europe's 'green battery'
- This represents a notable shift in Norway's energy policy stance toward fossil fuels over renewables


